 "text": "Hi, how are you doing these days? Of course. How old is your toddler? Lots of energy. Picking a park with lot of open space for running around is key. Small toddler hands get stuck in the thorns. A blanket for sitting on, and to eat off, and a blanket for each parent. Sticks and strings for stringing rice kernels, paper balls to tear apart, and a box of washable markers. A big blanket in the sun is nice, or shaded but still warm. Yes, for those mark a box marks. Also, keep an eye on sun exposure and get everyone off before skin starts to turn.",
